      "body_sha256": "52fc185f620a28a8fe7829e5a3d010f54c6313c272ce9dc1e859683377faec05",
      "title_en": "🇨🇦🇺🇸 Bead frames for North American switch plates: measurements that fit",
      "body_en": "A friend and I tested these measurements ourselves. The pieces are already on the wall and fit, so I am sharing them with other bead crafters in North America.\n\nPhotos 1–2 show a square double-switch plate, measuring 12 × 12 cm. Photos 3–4 show a rectangular single-switch plate, measuring 12.5 × 8 cm. Measure the plates in your own home; they are usually similar.\n\nAdapting an existing pattern to a North American switch plate\nFirst, work out the opening in the centre. The following measurements are for textured ironing, which flattens the beads a little with a bath cloth. For ordinary ironing, reduce the opening by one bead.\n\nFor a square double-switch plate, leave an opening of 49 × 49 beads.\nFor a rectangular single-switch plate, leave an opening of 51 × 33 beads.\nIn photo 1, I left 50 beads and there is a small gap, so 49 works better.\n\nNext, adapt the pattern. Make the upper design as usual. When you reach the frame, establish the first border line and extend it in both directions. Mark the four corners of the opening, then complete the frame. See photos 5–7.\n\nAnother little tip: as shown in photo 8, you can leave alternating gaps when filling the inside. With textured ironing, I found the result looked the same and was quicker to make, as long as the edges were fully filled.\n\nA pegboard with a printed grid is much easier to line up.\n\nFinally, thank you to @芙蝶结🎀 for the pattern.",
      "date": "2026-07-14"
    },
    {
      "id": "6a5194aa0000000002003c00",
      "title": "🇨🇦向朋友们分享我的拼豆小屋🏠😋",
      "body": "过去两个月一直在装饰我的拼豆home studio，趁毕业季搬了新家，腾出了一个空房间。上个月海运的快递也到哩，这种彩色系毛毡板真的超好看，推荐！现在就差把它们填满了，拼豆女工即刻上线[哇R]\n我买的毛毡板是30厘米的正方形，每块间隔20厘米。背后贴的魔术贴特别牢固，再贴层美纹纸就不会伤墙皮了。\n#拼豆创意美学[话题]# #howto装扮我的家[话题]# #拼豆实用主义[话题]# #加拿大[话题]# #汉密尔顿[话题]# #毛毡板[话题]# #毛毡板装饰[话题]# #拼豆[话题]# #小破烂大改造[话题]##拼豆店[话题]#",
